[list]
[*]Outfit Stands Plus' mechanized and mending stands now work as shift stands. Shift changes run at their boosted swap speeds, and the mending stand repairs a borrower's parked clothes while they are on shift.
[*]One Set owner per stand when Outfit Stands Plus is installed: a stand in service for shift changes shows this mod's owner control, and a stand set to Not used for shift changes shows theirs. Each mod keeps its own assignments either way.
[*]The work-type button now reads its state on its face — "Shift stand: doctoring", "Not used for shift changes" — and its dialog names what the game currently reads the room as. That explains the odd cases: a hospital with a crib in it stops dressing doctors because the game calls that room a barracks.
[*]Allow removing items holds itself off while a stand is in service: turned on, the stand's contents are exposed to every colonist's outfit optimizer, and owning the stand does not protect them. A stand already on stays switchable, and setting Not used for shift changes unlocks the toggle for decommissioning.
[/list]
